 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Robot groundskeeper B-12 sanded every golf ball at Mossy Pines perfectly smooth.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 4.725
  },
  {
   "text": "At noon: the Club Championship. First prize: a golden toaster.",
   "s": 4.925,
   "e": 8.043
  },
  {
   "text": "B-12 thought the dimples were dents. It buffed each ball until it reflected the clouds.",
   "s": 8.243,
   "e": 12.31
  },
  {
   "text": "Then Margaret \"The Hurricane\" Pratt teed off with her famous drive.",
   "s": 12.51,
   "e": 15.431
  },
  {
   "text": "Her ball flew half as far, plopped into the pond, and a duck kept it.",
   "s": 15.631,
   "e": 18.612
  },
  {
   "text": "Next golfer: same. The third golfer hit the snack cart.",
   "s": 18.812,
   "e": 21.365
  },
  {
   "text": "B-12's fix: polish them shinier. The next ball barely cleared the golfer's shoe.",
   "s": 21.565,
   "e": 25.611
  },
  {
   "text": "By three o'clock, the pond held ninety-two balls, and the duck was sitting on them like eggs.",
   "s": 25.811,
   "e": 29.174
  },
  {
   "text": "So why does a smooth ball quit early?",
   "s": 29.374,
   "e": 30.923
  },
  {
   "text": "It drags a big, messy whirlpool of air behind it, like a parachute.",
   "s": 31.223,
   "e": 34.375
  },
  {
   "text": "Dimples make the air hug the ball, so the whirlpool shrinks. The ball flies twice as far.",
   "s": 34.575,
   "e": 38.789
  },
  {
   "text": "B-12 learned fast. Now it adds dimples to everything.",
   "s": 39.189,
   "e": 41.881
  },
  {
   "text": "Including the golden toaster. Toast now flies twice as far.",
   "s": 42.081,
   "e": 45.374
  }
 ],
